      "question_number": 52,
      "question_text": "52 A reaction between copper and nitric acid produces a blue solution of copper(II) nitrate, water and substance X only. Substance X does not contain copper or hydrogen. The balanced equation for the reaction shows that 1 mole of copper reacts to produce 2 moles of water. What is the identity of substance X?",
