      "correct_answer": "C",
      "raw_text": "52   A reaction between copper and nitric acid produces a blue solution of copper(II) nitrate, water\n     and substance X only.\n     Substance X does not contain copper or hydrogen.\n     The balanced equation for the reaction shows that 1 mole of copper reacts to produce 2 moles\n     of water.\n     What is the identity of substance X?\n     A   N2\n     B   NO\n     C   NO2\n     D   NO3\n     E   N2O5",
      "diagram_images": []
    },
